        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: Michigan gubernatorial election, 2006\n- People: Jennifer Granholm, Dick DeVos, Ruth Johnson, Porter Hazelton\n- Roles: Governor of Michigan, lieutenant governor candidate, businessman, author, politician, Michigan House of Representatives member\n- Places: Michigan, United States\n\nFacts:\n- Porter Hazelton was a Michigan politician who lived from November 15, 1812, to August 15, 1870.\n- Dick DeVos was born on October 21, 1955, and is an American entrepreneur, businessman, and author from Michigan.\n- The Michigan gubernatorial election of 2006 was one of 36 U.S. gubernatorial elections held on November 7, 2006.\n- In the 2006 Michigan gubernatorial election, incumbent Democratic Governor Jennifer Granholm was re-elected over Republican businessman Dick DeVos and three minor party candidates.\n- Ruth Johnson was a former member of the Michigan House of Representatives and was the 2006 Republican candidate for lieutenant governor as Dick DeVos's running mate.",
